******************* R E S O N A N C E  R A N G E *****************7231 1451   29
                                                                  7231 1451   30
 Authors: T Ware, M Moxon, D Weaver, C Dean and R Hiles           7231 1451   31
 November 2009 (SERCO)                                            7231 1451   32
                                                                  7231 1451   33
 The parameters in this isotopic evaluation were generated as     7231 1451   34
 part of an evaluation of natural Hafnium data. This isotopic     7231 1451   35
 evaluation should be used with those for the other isotopes that 7231 1451   36
 form this evaluation of natural Hf data.                         7231 1451   37
                                                                  7231 1451   38
 The parameters for resonances in MF 2 (resolved resonance        7231 1451   39
 region) are based on the analysis presented in Ref.1. and        7231 1451   40
 summarised in Ref.2. The resolved region was analyzed in Reich-  7231 1451   41
 Moore formalism by T. Ware using the REFIT analysis              7231 1451   42
 code (Ref.3.). It is supplemented by two studies by M. Moxon.    7231 1451   43
 The first reviewed published thermal (2200m/s) capture cross     7231 1451   44
 sections, adjusted appropriate measurements to modern standards  7231 1451   45
 and inverse variance weighted the results. The second (Ref.4.)   7231 1451   46
 used the REFIT code to fit resonance parameters for the 7.8eV    7231 1451   47
 doublet where resonances in Hf-176 and Hf-178 overlap.           7231 1451   48
 Analysis for natural Hf by T Ware results in resonance           7231 1451   49
 parameters for each of the naturally occurring isotopes. In all, 7231 1451   50
 24 measurements are included in the final fit. Six existing      7231 1451   51
 natural hafnium transmission measurements by P Siegler           7231 1451   52
 (Ref.5.) were complemented by six capture measurements specially 7231 1451   53
 performed for the evaluation by P Schillebeeckx and colleagues   7231 1451   54
 using GELINA at IRMM GEEL (Ref.6.). A further natural            7231 1451   55
 transmission measurement on a thick 16mm sample was made in 2009 7231 1451   56
 at Geel and included in the fit to help define the scattering    7231 1451   57
 radius. To attribute resonances to isotopes 10 further capture   7231 1451   58
 measurements were made at GELINA using HfO2 samples enriched in  7231 1451   59
 Hf-176, 177, 178 and 179 and loaned by IRNE Sofia. As no samples 7231 1451   60
 enriched in Hf-180 were available, Moxon's 1973 Harwell capture  7231 1451   61
 measurement was included (Ref.7.). Other ORNL( Harvey - Ref.8.), 7231 1451   62
 Harwell (Moxon - Ref.7.) and RPI (Trbovich - Ref.9.) data were   7231 1451   63
 used to validate the measurements applied in the fit.            7231 1451   64
 The current fits to Hf result in parameters for the following    7231 1451   65
 ranges:-                                                         7231 1451   66
     Isotope      Resolved range     Unresolved range             7231 1451   67
                                                                  7231 1451   68
