##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           7231 1451  245
                                                                  7231 1451  246
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    7231 1451  247
discrete levels.                                                  7231 1451  248
                                                                  7231 1451  249
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         7231 1451  250
                                                                  7231 1451  251
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  7231 1451  252
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   7231 1451  253
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      7231 1451  254
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  7231 1451  255
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      7231 1451  256
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         7231 1451  257
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   7231 1451  258
on an angular grid.                                               7231 1451  259
                                                                  7231 1451  260
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       7231 1451  261
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        7231 1451  262
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         7231 1451  263
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         7231 1451  264
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         7231 1451  265
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        7231 1451  266
                                                                  7231 1451  267
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     7231 1451  268
                                                                  7231 1451  269
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     7231 1451  270
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   7231 1451  271
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  7231 1451  272
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             7231 1451  273
All data are generated with TALYS.                                7231 1451  274
                                                                  7231 1451  275
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   7231 1451  276
                                                                  7231 1451  277
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      7231 1451  278
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   7231 1451  279
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   7231 1451  280
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are7231 1451  281
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   7231 1451  282
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  7231 1451  283
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              7231 1451  284
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 7231 1451  285
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  7231 1451  286
For each residual product:                                        7231 1451  287
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               7231 1451  288
- the recoil                                                      7231 1451  289
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         7231 1451  290
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     7231 1451  291
sections.                                                         7231 1451  292
                                                                  7231 1451  293
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     7231 1451  294
                                                                  7231 1451  295
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  7231 1451  296
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 7231 1451  297
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          7231 1451  298
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       7231 1451  299
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 7231 1451  300
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     7231 1451  301
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  7231 1451  302
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      7231 1451  303
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         7231 1451  304
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             7231 1451  305
                                                                  7231 1451  306
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   7231 1451  307
followed:                                                         7231 1451  308
                                                                  7231 1451  309
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         7231 1451  310
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         7231 1451  311
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         7231 1451  312
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     7231 1451  313
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     7231 1451  314
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     7231 1451  315
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     7231 1451  316
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     7231 1451  317
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     7231 1451  318
                                                                  7231 1451  319
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 7231 1451  320
                                                                  7231 1451  321
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    7231 1451  322
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          7231 1451  323
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     7231 1451  324
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          7231 1451  325
                                                                  7231 1451  326
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  7231 1451  327
                                                                  7231 1451  328
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     7231 1451  329
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    7231 1451  330
as isomer.                                                        7231 1451  331
                                                                  7231 1451  332
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 7231 1451  333
                                                                  7231 1451  334
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        7231 1451  335
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    7231 1451  336
as isomer.                                                        7231 1451  337
                                                                  7231 1451  338
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          7231 1451  339
                                                                  7231 1451  340
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:7231 1451  341
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   7231 1451  342
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   7231 1451  343
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   7231 1451  344
  given                                                           7231 1451  345
                                                                  7231 1451  346
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          7231 1451  347
                                                                  7231 1451  348
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  7231 1451  349
                                                                  7231 1451  350
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 7231 1451  351
                                                                  7231 1451  352
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         7231 1451  353
                                                                  7231 1451  354
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   7231 1451  355
                                                                  7231 1451  356
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        7231 1451  357
and more details are given above in this description.             7231 1451  358
                                                                  7231 1451  359
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 7231 1451  360
                                                                  7231 1451  361
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  7231 1451  362
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     7231 1451  363
with the TASMAN code (Ref. 11), which generates TALYS runs using  7231 1451  364
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   7231 1451  365
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  7231 1451  366
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                7231 1451  367
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      7231 1451  368
   same reaction channel between different energies)              7231 1451  369
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      7231 1451  370
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               7231 1451  371
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      7231 1451  372
   different reaction channels for different energies)            7231 1451  373
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        7231 1451  374
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              7231 1451  375
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  7231 1451  376
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       7231 1451  377
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     7231 1451  378
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  7231 1451  379
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     7231 1451  380
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     7231 1451  381
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     7231 1451  382
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   7231 1451  383
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   7231 1451  384
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  7231 1451  385
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   7231 1451  386
                                                                  7231 1451  387
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  7231 1451  388
                                                                  7231 1451  389
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       7231 1451  390
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  7231 1451  391
are generated with the TASMAN code (Ref. 11), which generates     7231 1451  392
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   7231 1451  393
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         7231 1451  394
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  7231 1451  395
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      7231 1451  396
representation is used.                                           7231 1451  397
                                                                  7231 1451  398
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      7231 1451  399
                                                                  7231 1451  400
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  7231 1451  401
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             7231 1451  402
                                                                  7231 1451  403
